    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Cha Cha Cha is the third studio album by EMF, released in 1995 on EMI/Parlophone. Marking a clear shift from the band’s early breakthrough sound, the record leans more toward a darker, less immediately commercial blend of electronic textures and rock dynamics, reflecting EMF’s attempt to move beyond the upbeat dance-rock formula associated with Unbelievable.\n\nThe album includes the singles “Perfect Day” and “Bleeding You Dry,” the latter often cited as the most accessible track on the set and one of the few moments that recalls the group’s earlier techno-pop energy. While it did not match the commercial success of EMF’s debut, Cha Cha Cha is notable as the band’s final full-length album of new material and as a document of their more experimental mid-1990s direction.",
